<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caribbean Community</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1973</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CARICOM</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> Community, CARICOM, is an organisation of Caribbean states and dependencies founded by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaguaramas">Chaguaramas</a> in 1973 to promote economic integration and cooperation in foreign policy, health and education. It succeeded the Caribbean Free Trade Association and revived the regional cooperation lost with the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation in 1962. Its secretariat is in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgetown-guyana">Georgetown, Guyana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caribbean-community.jpg" alt="Caribbean Community" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CARICOM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_CARICOM.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
